Third-party material in this repository

The MIT grant above covers the original work here: `crates/`, `nix/`,
`badge/app/`, `badge/probe/`, `badge/*.py`, `badge/*.sh`, `check.sh`,
`flake.nix`, and the documentation.

It does **not** cover the following, which are derived from or produced by
other projects:

1. `badge/*.patch`
   Unified diffs against `betrusted-io/xous-core` at commit
   9844906ddc1214438d0d942d2db2922846ae4722. Each file contains context lines
   and modified lines from that project's source, so the patches are derivative
   works of xous-core and carry its license terms. See
   https://github.com/betrusted-io/xous-core for the authoritative license.
   The patches are written to be reported upstream and are offered back to that
   project under whatever terms it uses.

2. `prebuilt/loader.uf2` and `prebuilt/xous.uf2`
   Compiled from xous-core at the revision above (with four of the patches in
   `badge/*.patch` applied), signed with xous-core's development key. These are
   xous-core binaries; they carry that project's license terms.
   `prebuilt/swap.uf2` is this project's application packed into xous-core's
   swap-image container format.

3. `docs/xous-api-notes.md`
   Contains verbatim quotations from xous-core source, each cited by file and
   line. Quoted for the purpose of documenting an API; the quoted lines remain
   under xous-core's license.

4. `nix/` build outputs
   Nothing under `nix/` vendors third-party source. It builds a Linux kernel
   (GPL-2.0) and a busybox userland (GPL-2.0) from nixpkgs; those artifacts are
   not distributed here and carry their own licenses when you build them.

5. `badge/logs/*`
   Captured hardware transcripts. They contain kernel and firmware output from
   Linux, xous-core and this project, reproduced as diagnostic evidence.

Nothing in this repository redistributes the DEF CON 34 badge's stock firmware.
